# Lift

> Treat the open internet, or any one URL, as an ai::Model.

## Purpose
Explain lift as a way to point at the web and use that page as if it were a model. Source: fitzyracing1/lift.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Name a URL or the open internet.
2. Lift that target into the model slot.
3. Ask the model slot as you would ask a local model.
4. Keep the C++ interface small.

## Key ideas
- ai::Model (the named slot a model sits in)
- Lift (put a URL into that slot)
- Open internet (the large target when no single URL is named)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/lift
model = lift(url_or_internet)
ask(model)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. model = lift(...) → “put that web target in the model slot”
2. ask(model) → “query it like a model”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a URL is named → lift that page
- If no URL is named → lift the open internet

## What a person would notice
A website treated as something you can ask.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open fitzyracing1/lift and point it at one URL.
